==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|süss}} {{qualifier|Switzerland}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|suozi}} (akin to Old Saxon {{m|osx|swōti}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*swōtuz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*sweh₂dus}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|sööt}}, Dutch {{m|nl|zoet}}, English {{m|en|sweet}}, Danish {{m|da|sød}}.

